# {{project_name}} — Symphony Assistant

This project uses [Symphony](https://github.com/ivanzzeth/symphony), an AI-powered development orchestrator.
Symphony tracks work via Linear issues, dispatches AI agents from `Todo` issues, and manages the full dev lifecycle.

## Issue Lifecycle

| State | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| `Backlog` | Parked work, ignored by Symphony |
| `Todo` | Queued for agent dispatch |
| `In Progress` | Agent actively working |
| `In Review` | PR attached, waiting for human review |
| `Merging` | Approved, agent executing merge |
| `Rework` | Reviewer requested changes |
| `Done` / `Canceled` / `Duplicate` | Terminal |

## Skills

| Skill | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `symphony-linear` | Linear GraphQL operations (state transitions, comments, issue creation) |
| `symphony-commit` | Create well-formed git commits |
| `symphony-push` | Push branch, create/update PR |
| `symphony-pull` | Sync branch with origin/base |
| `symphony-land` | Squash-merge PR (sweep + merge modes) |
| `symphony-debug` | Investigate stuck/failing runs |
| `symphony-harness` | Configure and maintain agent harness |

## Variables

Project-specific variables in `.agents/symphony-vars.yaml` must be replaced before first agent run.

## Directory Structure

```
.agents/
├── agents/                        # Agent definitions
│   └── symphony-*.md
├── skills/
│   ├── symphony-*/                # Symphony generic skills
│   │   └── SKILL.md
│   └── <project>-*/               # Project-specific skills
├── templates/
│   ├── WORKFLOW.md.symphony       # Workflow definition template
│   └── AGENTS.md.symphony         # This file template
├── symphony-vars.yaml             # Project variables
└── .symphony-manifest.yaml        # Version manifest (managed by `symphony init`)
```
